As members of Teneo’s Transactions & Strategic Situations team head to the 38th Annual Tulane Corporate Law Institute, we’re anticipating 4 key themes will dominate the conversation:
 
1) Deal volume will increase, dictated by capital cost consciousness;
2) Increasing variance in shareholder activism voting expectations;
3) Antitrust considerations remain critical, and are more complex than ever;
4) AI remains the critical factor for demonstrating anticipation and readiness.
 
Find our Teneo representatives about town.

Stephen Cohen, TJ White, Justin Kane, Alexander E. Miehls

In the latest episode of the Earned First podcast, our Asia-Pacific Head of Intelligence and Transformation, Red Surtida, joins founding editor Arun Sudhaman and research & insights editor David B. to unpack findings from The Credibility Paradox study which shifts the GEO conversation from visibility to credibility.
 
The conversation explores:
☑️Why visibility alone shouldn't be the end game;
☑️Why leadership content is underperforming as a credibility signal;
☑️How employee experience is emerging as a critical reputation asset;
☑️Why channel effectiveness varies dramatically across industries and markets; and
☑️How can brands overcome language barriers in AI environments
 
As AI reshapes how audiences discover, evaluate and believe brands, understanding the new drivers of credibility has never been more important.
 
